清洁电力
China has unveiled an action plan to speed up the building of a "new electricity system" as part of the country's efforts to pursue low-carbon development and ensure energy security. Chinese authorities will work to increase the transmission of clean electricity through the grid using advanced power generation, regulation and control technologies. As wind and solar power generation in China's deserts and desertified areas is increasing, there is a growing need to transmit the clean energy to electricity-consuming regions. China aims to raise the total installed capacity of wind and solar power generation facilities in deserts and desertified areas to 455 million kilowatts by 2030. Currently, cross-regional transmission lines mainly transport coal and hydro power.